  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This strange-leafed small compact upright dwarf grows to about 2 ft. (60 cm) in five years or so. It resembles a dwarf form of 'Wabito' with similar dark green leaves. These are small and very deeply divided into fine narrow almost straplike lobes. The often red-tinged margins are unevenly and bluntly toothed and crinkled. The name means \"hippopotamus\", a play on the name of the English nursery from where it originated."
  },
